>
  <p>
    Ivins writes more design rules into its fence and wall code than its neighbors do. Beyond height limits, it regulates front
    courtyard walls, block color along its main streets, and which materials are allowed at all. Anyone quoting a fence or wall in
    Ivins should know these; this page summarizes Ivins City Code §16.11.135 and §16.11.136 as read on September 26, 2026.
  </p>

  <h2>Ivins fence and wall rules at a glance</h2>
  <IconList items={rules} />

  <h2>Front courtyard walls</h2>
  <p>
    A courtyard wall encloses an open-air patio in the front yard. Ivins allows them, with conditions: they must sit at least 10
    feet behind the back of the sidewalk (7 feet 6 inches in gated developments), at least 5 feet from the side property line, and
    front-facing courtyard walls 10 to 15 feet from the front property line are limited to 4 feet 6 inches, with side-facing walls
    15 feet or more back limited to 5 feet 6 inches. Gates may be up to 6 feet 6 inches. A building permit with a plot plan and
    elevations is required.
  </p>

  <h2>Retaining walls in Ivins</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A retaining wall over 4 feet may not have its exposed face toward a public or private street, unless it is hidden by a building, structure, or fencing.</li>
    <li>Walls over 4 feet must be terraced, with at least a 3-foot offset face to face.</li>
    <li>Within 10 feet of a development's boundary, a wall over 4 feet above existing grade needs the adjacent owner's written approval.</li>
    <li>Walls must be built or finished to blend with the surrounding landscape colors.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    See the <a href="/retaining-wall-cost-st-george-ut/">retaining wall cost guide</a> for what terracing, drainage, and
    engineering add to a budget.
  </p>

  <h2>Pools</h2>
  <p>
    §16.11.135 includes its own requirement for fencing around private swimming pools, hot tubs, and similar pools. Read that
    subsection or ask the city before you choose a pool fence, and see our <a href="/pool-fence-and-gate-st-george-ut/">pool fence
    guide</a> for the questions to ask.
  </p>

  <h2>What it costs</h2>
  <p>
    No Ivins fence or wall company publishes prices. As of {COST_AS_OF}, typical residential fence projects in the St. George area
    run about {fenceProject.low}–{fenceProject.high} installed, and CMU block walls about {blockWall.perSqFt} per square foot. If your wall
    needs Ivins' required block color, a split-face row, or terracing, ask each company to price those items explicitly. The <a href="/fence-and-block-wall-cost-st-george-ut/">cost guide</a> lists every source.
  </p>

